1
00:00:00,472 --> 00:00:04,061
In the age of AI, a dashboard
is just a few prompts away.

2
00:00:04,344 --> 00:00:08,122
Anyone can vibe-code one in minutes.

3
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:10,400
So they multiply.

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:14,010
Copies of copies,
each with its own version of the truth.

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,810
At Bayer's scale,
that is almost impossible to govern.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,400
Then the person who built
a critical dashboard leaves.

7
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,200
One day it breaks,

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,700
and nobody knows where its data comes from,
or how to fix it.

9
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:33,800
In Bayer's synthetic estate, 86 of 360 dashboards
already have no active owner.

10
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,800
Bonsai keeps analytics small, healthy, and owned.

11
00:00:38,316 --> 00:00:40,529
Day one, before any migration:

12
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:44,745
Bonsai scans the whole estate,
finds duplicates through their KPIs,

13
00:00:44,955 --> 00:00:47,695
checks who actually uses each dashboard,

14
00:00:47,906 --> 00:00:51,489
and suggests what to merge or retire.
So you only move what earns its place.

15
00:00:51,991 --> 00:00:54,414
Then every new request follows four rules.

16
00:00:54,705 --> 00:00:56,546
One: find before you build.

17
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:03,912
Bonsai searches what already exists, flags conflicting
KPI definitions, and proposes to build only the real gap.

18
00:01:04,509 --> 00:01:07,429
Two: nothing gets built without a human.

19
00:01:07,637 --> 00:01:11,391
The AI can only propose.
A regional Lead approves.

20
00:01:11,933 --> 00:01:15,147
Three: every number shows where it came from.

21
00:01:15,368 --> 00:01:20,245
Its definition, its semantic model, the exact SQL.

22
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:24,678
So when something breaks, anyone can fix it.

23
00:01:25,218 --> 00:01:30,196
Four: every dashboard has an owner,
and must earn its next ninety days.

24
00:01:30,408 --> 00:01:34,221
When an owner leaves, a data steward takes over.

25
00:01:34,767 --> 00:01:36,437
And governance runs on its own.

26
00:01:36,604 --> 00:01:40,777
Scheduled jobs watch every change,
flag new duplicates,

27
00:01:40,944 --> 00:01:43,281
and keep every finding up to date,

28
00:01:43,448 --> 00:01:49,124
so your team can focus on the questions that matter.

29
00:01:49,903 --> 00:01:53,903
Bonsai. Find before you build.

30
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:58,792
Govern what you keep.
